.TITLE "passwd"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Changes the password for a user account. It is the standard tool for __managing authentication__ and maintaining system security.

.DIV "TLDR"
**passwd**
Prompts the current user to change their own login password.
> 

**sudo passwd user**
Allows a superuser to change the password for a specific user account.
> __user__ the target username

**passwd -d user**
Removes the password for a user, effectively disabling the password requirement.
> __-d__ delete password flag | __user__ the target username

**passwd -l user**
Locks a user account, preventing them from logging in.
> __-l__ lock account flag | __user__ the target username

.DIV "SUMMARY"
For security reasons, the characters you type while entering a password will not be displayed on the screen. Always choose a __strong password__ with a mix of letters, numbers, and symbols to protect your account.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:useradd** **linux:usermod** **linux:shadow**

documentation: __https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/passwd.1.html__
